**How to implement.** The Library's 'By kind' grouping is derived from the entries it holds, so no grouping tree is seed data (the S1.7 brief: 'the By kind grouping is DERIVED by a pure function over the library's entries (kind, then category / facet, then leaf)'; .spec-md §3.3 'grouping trees' are deleted). `liveLibrary` and its one product consumer, the `model.library.libraryTrees ()` match in `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` (`libraryState`), keep their shapes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, type `LibraryTree`: `static member byKind (entries : LibraryEntry list) : LibraryTree`, pure, with a doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S1.7. Its name is `TreeName "By kind"` and its root `Group (TreeLabel "Library", groups)`. The groups are `Samples`, `Sources`, `Detectors` and `Polarizers`, in that order, and a kind with no entry has no group. Under `Samples`, one group per `SubstrateKind` present, in the order `Thin films` (`ThinFilm`), `Thick plates` (`ThickPlate`) and `Mirrors` (`Mirror`). Under `Sources`, `Fixed lines` (`FixedLine`) and then `Tunable` (`TunableBetween`). Under `Polarizers`, one group per `PolarizerCategory` present, in the union's case order, labelled by its `label`. Detectors carry no facet, so their leaves sit directly under `Detectors`. A leaf is `Leaf (entry.entryName.toTreeLabel, entry.entryId)`, and the leaves keep the order of the entries given. (2) `liveLibrary` (`ElementId.fs:liveLibrary`): `libraryTrees` answers `[ LibraryTree.byKind entries ]`, where the entries are those its own `entriesForKind` offers for `CatalogueKind.Sample`, `LightSource`, `Detector`, `LinearPolarizer` and `CircularPolarizer`, distinct by `entryId`; the first listing error passes through, as `entriesForKind`'s does. So a sample created in the samples store and a user source join the tree. Its doc's '`libraryTrees` stays the seeded grouping' says the tree is derived. (3) `createInMemoryEmpty` (`ElementId.fs:createInMemoryEmpty`): the store's `libraryTrees` answers `Ok [ LibraryTree.byKind held ]` over the entries it holds, in place of `Ok []`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, `createInMemory`: the bundle's `libraryEntries` is the store's own `proxy` again; step 42's override that answered the seeded tree (`(Library.createInMemory ()).libraryTrees`) and its doc line are deleted. The self-seeding `createInMemory` keeps `seedTrees` until step 58. No other grouping, ordering or option is added. (5) Facts, in `LibraryProxyTests`: `the By kind tree groups entries by kind, then facet, then leaf`: `LibraryTree.byKind` over a test-local list (the fixture's `SampleIds.glassFilm200Id` thin film and `SampleIds.euvMoSiId` mirror as `SampleItem`s, `PresetIds.heNe633` and `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator` from `BuiltinCatalogue.preset`, the ellipsometer, and the linear and left circular polarizers) equals the expected tree written out in the fact, and over `[]` it is the root with no group; `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds`: `Library.createInMemoryEmpty ()` answers the empty tree, and after `addEntry` of the intensity detector a tree with that one leaf under `Detectors`; `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`, with a user source saved under `newSourceId ()` and a sample saved under `newSampleId ()`, the leaf ids of `liveLibrary`'s tree are exactly the distinct entry ids `entriesForKind` offers for the five kinds, each once, both new entries included. In `LibraryControlsTests`: `the Select bay lists a sample created in the samples store under its geometry`: over `initMain ()`, a copy of `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.euvMoSiId` (a `Mirror`) under `newSampleId ()` and a test-local name, saved in the scene's `samples` store, appears with a Sample element selected as a leaf row of `libraryState` under the `Mirrors` group row.

**Acceptance.** After the derivation, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs` MUST NOT call the self-seeding `Library.createInMemory`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the By kind tree groups entries by kind, then facet, then leaf`, `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds` and `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once`; ui-smoke MUST pass, the Select-bay re-render fact included; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Select bay lists a sample created in the samples store under its geometry` and LibraryControlsTests' Select-bay facts; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
